399: // An ArrayBuffer::Allocator class with some Node.js-specific tweaks. If you do
400: // not have to use another allocator, using this class is recommended:
401: // - It supports Buffer.allocUnsafe() and Buffer.allocUnsafeSlow() with
402: //   uninitialized memory.
403: // - It supports transferring, rather than copying, ArrayBuffers when using
404: //   MessagePorts.
405: class NODE_EXTERN ArrayBufferAllocator : public v8::ArrayBuffer::Allocator {
